  "id": "COMPOUND:20046 - PROTEIN:5757",
  "verbalization": "Phytolaccoside B is shown to interact with multiple downstream targets that ultimately lead to a relationship with Y79. The drug is identified as a target for three distinct kinases: Tubulin beta-2A chain, Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 13, and Serine/threonine-protein kinase ULK2. These targets are all involved in signaling pathways that are implicated in cellular processes such as proliferation, survival, and metabolism. The shared downstream target of all three kinases is the compound (1S,2S,5R,6R,7S,8S,11S)-7-hydroxy-5-(hydroxymethyl)-11-[(2R)-1-hydroxypropan-2-yl]-6-methyl-9-oxatricyclo[6.2.1.02,6]undecan-10-one, which is further linked to Y79. This suggests that Phytolaccoside B may modulate a common signaling network that influences Y79's function. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Phytolaccoside B and Y79 through the inhibition of key signaling pathways, though the exact mode of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
